Z||000000||Stage-2GT||10-06-2001||06:15 PM||||  I need new speakers for my 887GT. The ones in the panel behind the seats, any recommendations? Also, if anyone has any that are out, could you measure the true depth for me? I would greatly appreciate it. <P>Thanks!!<P>S2GT <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||sqoach||10-06-2001||06:49 PM||||I would recommend going with a 4x6 plate. It has a seperate 4" woofer and tweeter. Some of them allow you to re-locate the tweeter. Read in a crutchfield magazine the mounting depth is 1 3/4" but I have a pair that are 1 7/8" that fit. However, the foam is not there, so that's probably why they fit. I've heard the Infinity Kappa plates are really nice, and I believe the mounting depth is 1 3/4". I think crutchfield still has them on sale for $89.99 so you might want to check them out.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Stage-2GT||10-06-2001||08:37 PM||||  Danka Sqoach, Anyone else have any info for me???<P>S2GT <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000003||mshill||10-06-2001||09:31 PM||||Along the lines of replacing the 4x6 speakers, my son is completely restoring the interior of his 85 SE that had speakers in the seats.  He wants to put a  pair of legacy plates in the 4x6 location.<P>Do all fieros have speaker cutouts in the frame of the b-pillar?  If not I don't know if I want to start ripping things out just yet.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||10-06-2001||09:35 PM||||First, All 4X6 plates have a 3 1/2" woofer and seperate tweeter. Not a 4" woofer.<BR>I put a seperate 4" woofer and panel mounted the tweeter.<P>They sound excellent.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Speaker_set.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||10-06-2001||11:59 PM||||don't like the location myself. i use one rear center speaker in my '87 (experimenting. i like it but won't recommend it) and will probaly just leave them disconnected in my '86 or look for some '84-5 seats.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||10-07-2001||12:05 AM||||I just slapped a pair of FanaticX 4" mids in the rear, and x'd them over. Sounds G-r-r-r-r-r-eat!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||sqoach||10-07-2001||12:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR><B>First, All 4X6 plates have a 3 1/2" woofer and seperate tweeter. Not a 4" woofer.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Oops. My bad. I thought I remember seeing where it was a 4" woofer. Oh well. I was close  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>mshill, I don't think the 84/85 fieros have a hole back there. You'd have to do some cutting, which I think would be a PITA.||||reg||1
Z||000008||86seyellow||10-07-2001||10:00 AM||||Do it the right way. the back speakers wont produce alot of sound expcept to hightlight your tunes. I put 6x9 boxes behind the driver and passenger seats mounted witha angle iron . they dont block anything since it is in the blind spot anyhow. Cops cant tell they are speaker boxes cause the fir exactly behind the headrest. I am running all jensen including a 10" sub. I prefer the 6x9 tris in the back. Now my tunes have power every direction. Lots of pwoer too<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86seyellow_new1.JPG">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1_copy1.jpg"> <BR>I can go as fast as I want unless I get caught||||reg||1
Z||000009||Philphine||10-07-2001||10:00 AM||||actually, someone dose or did make a 4x6 with a 4" woofer. i remember considering it back when i was putting stuff in my '87 or maybe my chevys (4x6 fronts in car and truck). don't know if it would be worth digging around to find out who though. <P>if you're a junkmonger and you've got some old crutchfields laying around i think it will be in there. might luck out and some shop has a set collecting dust on a shelf you can get cheap if they're discontiued.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Oreif||10-07-2001||10:20 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>actually, someone dose or did make a 4x6 with a 4" woofer. i remember considering it back when i was putting stuff in my '87 or maybe my chevys (4x6 fronts in car and truck). don't know if it would be worth digging around to find out who though. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yes, ADS made/makes a set of 4X6's with a 4" woofer but due to speaker placement and the size of the magnet you cannot fit them in the sail panels.<P><BR>Also putting 6X9's behind the seat headrests would cause you to lose the front staging/imaging of the stereo system.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||86seyellow||10-07-2001||10:53 AM||||The way I have my system set with the sub woofer and fronts and rears(6x9) it is perfect. I pride myself with perfect balance. I used to own part of a hoem theater store and I have been doing car audio for 15 years. You amy be right Oreif, but I like it and it is just right for a 2 seater<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86seyellow_new1.JPG">    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fieropix1_copy1.jpg"> <BR>I can go as fast as I want unless I get caught||||reg||1
Z||000012||Mach10||10-07-2001||02:13 PM||||86: Never did like 6x9s... I prefer round speakers, much cleaner sound. I have my fronts and rears cut out at 100Hz. I wouldn't ever mount speakers like that, it clutters up the cabin, IMHO. Bet it's LOUD though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm a major proponent of spending the most time and effort up front, (a good pair of 5"1/4s will fit perfectly up front) and using the rear only for mids/bass. I can't STAND having tweeters behind me, screws up the imaging. I'm really happy with my 4" mid-onlys in the back, and my Premier 5'1/4s up front. I have my 10" sub kicking out up to 125hz in the foot well, firing into the cabin, so I can push a little mid through it, and not mess up the staging...||||reg||6
Z||000013||Oreif||10-07-2001||04:49 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 86seyellow:<BR><B>The way I have my system set with the sub woofer and fronts and rears(6x9) it is perfect. I pride myself with perfect balance. I used to own part of a hoem theater store and I have been doing car audio for 15 years. You amy be right Oreif, but I like it and it is just right for a 2 seater<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First, If you worked/owned a Home thearter store, You would understand what the difference is between front stage and how it plays an important role in imaging a system. Because the Fiero is a 2-seater and there is no back seat to add distance, Imaging is harder. A 6X9 behind your head is not a "balanced" system. It's just loud. There is nothing wrong with the way you did your system. If you like it, that is what is important to you. Some folks just like it loud and some folks like to listen to the music. Acoustic clarity was the goal I set out to meet when I did my system. I think I have succeeded in doing it.<P>BTW ~ I've been doing car audio systems since 1979. <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Areakon||10-07-2001||11:59 PM||||How well do the 4" speakers do for the low end of things? I wouldn't think they could do crap for bass.<P>------------------<BR>He who knows nothing, loves nothing. He who can do nothing understands nothing. He who understands nothing is worthless.<BR>              Paracelsus||||reg||1
Z||000015||Joe Torma||10-08-2001||12:39 AM||||4" are useless for bass.  I have them and use them pretty much to fill in highs/mids in the rear.  Get some bass blockers or set the HPF to where they don't distort...probably 125hz<P>For Sound Quality, you want all the good stuff from the front.  you try to get the vocals and instruments accurately placed in front of you.  ||||reg||1
